w"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>4808664</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-5807937-A" status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5807937</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1197498A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJITA NAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook> </applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KANEGAFUCHI CHEMICAL IND</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook> </applicant> <applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITANO KENICHI</name> <address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAGAWA YOSHIKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJITA, NAO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANEKA CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITANO, KENICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAGAWA, YOSHIKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJITA NAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITANO KENICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAGAWA YOSHIKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJITA, NAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITANO, KENICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAGAWA, YOSHIKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A vinyl polymer having halogen groups at the ends is treated with a hydroxy anionic compound in order to remove the halogen groups therefrom.  The terminal halogen groups of the vinyl polymer can be easily removed.  Thus, the storage stability of the polymer itself or of a curable composition containing the polymer can be improved, and a reactor or various materials to come into contact with the polymer can be prevented from corroding.  In particular, a polymer having crosslinkable silyl groups can be made to have significantly improved storage stability.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>On traite ce polymère vinylique portant des groupes halogènes sur ses extrémités à l'aide d'un composé anionique hydroxy et ce, pour ôter les groupes halogènes, lesquels groupes halogènes terminaux sont facile à ôter. Il est, de la sorte possible d'améliorer la stabilité à l'entreposage du polymère lui-même ou d'une composition durcissable le contenant. Il est également possible de protéger contre la corrosion un réactif ou d'autres substances entrant en contact avec le polymère. Il est, notamment, possible d'améliorer de façon significative la stabilité à l'entreposage de polymères porteurs de groupes silyles réticulables.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval